Construct the known component $\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, ending at $A$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\overrightarrow{OA} &=1\,(5, 0)=(5, 0). \\
\overrightarrow{AC} &=(0, 14).
\end{aligned}
$$

![](assets/b94003120f234c53f0d3bf224a1ccea9b0c8cb44e77ecbd38fead47e93fff434.png)

Compare the remaining displacement with $\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(0, 4)$:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{Vertical scale} &=\frac{14}{4}=\frac{7}{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

The scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\overrightarrow{AC}=\frac{7}{2}\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{c} &=\overrightarrow{OA}+\overrightarrow{AC} \\
&=\mathbf{a}+\frac{7}{2}\mathbf{b} \\
&=\mathbf{a}+\frac{7}{2}\mathbf{b}.
\end{aligned}
$$

The vectors $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\mathbf{b}$ gives $\lambda=\frac{7}{2}$.

Construct the known component $\mathbf{b}$ from $O$, ending at $B$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\overrightarrow{OB} &=1\,(-5, 0)=(-5, 0). \\
\overrightarrow{BC} &=(0, 5).
\end{aligned}
$$

![](assets/41dc104ecafa12c066f3a5e0f26c2a6be376e8fe876d370a83e71c526c69f2dd.png)

Compare the remaining displacement with $\mathbf{a}$, whose grid displacement is $(0, 2)$:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{Vertical scale} &=\frac{5}{2}=\frac{5}{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

The scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\mathbf{a}$. Thus $\overrightarrow{BC}=\frac{5}{2}\mathbf{a}$. By the triangle law,

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{c} &=\overrightarrow{OB}+\overrightarrow{BC} \\
&=\mathbf{b}+\frac{5}{2}\mathbf{a} \\
&=\frac{5}{2}\mathbf{a}+\mathbf{b}.
\end{aligned}
$$

The vectors $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\mathbf{a}$ gives $\lambda=\frac{5}{2}$.
